   "shape_h": "blockquote",
   "shape_m": "blockquote",
   "html_text": "The cause and effect must be contiguous in space and time. The cause must be prior to the effect. There must be a constant union betwixt the cause and effects. It is chiefly this quality, that constitutes the relation. The same cause always produces the same effect, and the same effect never arises but from the same cause. This Principle we derive from experience, and is the source of most of our philosophical reasonings. For when by any clear experiment we have discovered the causes or effects ",
